+# Audio input regression test
+
+Run from the repository root after initializing `external/chiaki-ng`:
+
+```sh
+python3 native/tests/run_audio_decoder_input_test.py
+```
+
+Requirements: Linux host, Python 3, a C compiler with AddressSanitizer and
+UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer, pthreads, and the pinned core submodule. No Android
+SDK, PS5, or account is needed for this test.
+
+The test compiles the production `native/jni/audio-decoder.c` callback. A fake
+MediaCodec deterministically refuses the first input buffer or a later buffer;
+the real Chiaki mutex implementation is checked from another pthread after each
+return. Checking from the same thread would miss the bug because this decoder
+uses a recursive mutex. The normal submission case also verifies the bytes and
+timestamps passed into the codec.
+
+It covers:
+
+- calls before a codec exists;
+- timeout before any buffer is acquired;
+- timeout after part of a sample has been submitted;
+- successful submission without sample corruption.
+
+Use `--source /absolute/path/to/audio-decoder.c` to run the same test against
+another source revision. The unpatched 1.28.1-tv source fails the cross-thread
+mutex probe; the patched source passes all four cases.
+
+The `media-stubs/` declarations exist only for this host test. They are not
+included in the APK build. Sanitizers check the exercised host paths;
+LeakSanitizer is off by default because some sandbox tracers cannot run it.
+Callers can override `ASAN_OPTIONS`.
+
+This is not an APK build or a measurement of Android playback latency. Before
+deploying the accompanying fixes, build both ARM ABIs and validate on real
+devices: stream start/stop, background/resume, HEVC and AVC playback, audio
+backpressure/recovery, and primary L2/R2 press/release with a key-only controller.
+The new trigger notifications are limited to devices without the corresponding
+LTRIGGER/RTRIGGER motion axis (including a missing device). Analog-capable pads
+keep the existing motion-event notification path; verify partial presses on a
+DualSense as well. This does not change or fully validate the existing merging
+of digital and analog trigger state.
+For the API-30 low-latency request, inspect the selected codec's capabilities and
+compare enqueue-to-output and frame-presentation timing. A lower end-to-end
+latency must be demonstrated on the target TV rather than inferred from a key.
